<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Varig to sell stake in SATA.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Varig to sell stake in SATA.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian carrier Varig said it hopes to raise 90 million reais ($85.7 million) with the sale of its 80 percent stake in SATA, a local company in charge of ground services, a Varig spokesman said.</p>
<p>The sale is a part of a restructuring plan aimed at selling stakes in companies that are not part of Varig's core business, he added.</p>
<p>The spokesman also said that Varig was negotiating the sale with foreign companies but would not disclose further details.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
